{"chunk_id": "5335f7bebe4b", "text": "This section recounts the final moments and funeral of Bhishma after completing his long discourse on duty. Granted permission by Krishna, Bhishma consciously releases his life through yogic control, directing his life\u2011breath upward until it exits through the crown of his head and ascends to heaven, accompanied by celestial signs and praise from sages and gods. The Pandavas and elders perform his funeral rites with royal honors and cremate his body. Afterwards they go to the Ganges to offer libations. The river\u2011goddess Ganga rises from the waters, grieving for her son and recalling his unmatched valor and virtue. Krishna consoles her, reminding her that Bhishma was one of the divine Vasus who merely took human birth due to a curse and has now returned to the highest realm. The episode closes the Anusasana Parva, emphasizing Bhishma\u2019s sanctity, mastery over death, and his transition from heroic warrior to immortal exemplar of dharma.\nBhishma consciously releases his life through yogic control, is cremated with royal rites, and Krishna consoles the grieving goddess Ganga about her son\u2019s heavenly fate.\nThemes: Bhishma's death, yogic self-release, funeral rites, divine consolation, mother's grief", "vector": [0.0059815957210958, -0.012483039870858192, 0.0022610097657889128, -0.006274843588471413, -0.02493942156434059, 0.016901755705475807, -0.028045184910297394, -0.00784438755363226, -0.020407404750585556, -0.0029874653555452824, 0.009950442239642143, 0.022433482110500336, 0.015102279372513294, 0.010303673334419727, -0.011936532333493233, -0.013196166604757309, 0.04526684805750847, 0.0032273957040160894, 0.03452330455183983, -0.009550558403134346, 0.02047405205667019, 0.01502230204641819, -0.0026425656396895647, 0.025699200108647346, -0.01603534072637558, 0.021727021783590317, 0.026219049468636513, -0.0194610133767128, 0.004448707681149244, -0.01954098977148533, -0.008730797097086906, 0.0005365107790566981, -0.